{
  "description": "Shared vectors for sensor cuts (CAP-22): where a cut is drawn from and to, which side of its host's course a bearing is on, and which bearing keeping port or starboard keeps. debrief_kernel.sensors (with geodesy.TrackPath) and vscode/webview/sensors.ts must agree. relative: legacy Debrief's relBearing (the bearing less the course, within ±180°; every case of legacy's own test), port when below zero. default_length: a cut without a range is drawn twice the view's larger side, at most five degrees of arc (555,600 m). cases: a host track (coordinates, times) and cuts: each cut's origin is the position recorded with it, or the host's position at its time (as the map places tracks), null outside the host's span; course is the host's direction of travel then, as the map's pointAt gives it (null when it never moved); side is that of the bearing recorded first; lines are what is drawn (both bearings until resolved, then the one kept), each ending along the geodesic at its range (range_m) or the length it is drawn to (length_m); keep_port and keep_starboard say which bearing each keeps (null where there is no ambiguous bearing, or no course). Positions are [longitude, latitude] to within 1e-9 degrees, longitudes compared modulo 360; courses to within 1e-9 degrees.",
